#!/usr/bin/perl

use strict;
use warnings;
use v5.28.0;

=head1 NAME

list-amos-components - Discover and list available Protocol-7 console commands

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    bin/list-amos-components [OPTIONS] [ZENKA]

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Lists all available console commands across Protocol-7 zenka modules.
Commands register themselves via inline metadata in their source files.

=head1 OPTIONS

    --all              List all commands (default)
    --json             Output in JSON format (for AI/automation)
    --yaml             Output in YAML format
    --tag TAG          Filter by tag (e.g., development-tool, ai-friendly)
    --search PATTERN   Search command names and descriptions
    --zenka NAME       List commands from specific zenka
    --describe CMD     Show full documentation for command
    --version          Show version

=head1 EXAMPLES

    # List all available commands
    bin/list-amos-components

    # List all development tools
    bin/list-amos-components --tag development-tool

    # Search for workflow-related commands
    bin/list-amos-components --search workflow

    # Show commands in 'work' zenka
    bin/list-amos-components work

    # Get full documentation for a command
    bin/list-amos-components --describe work.ncode-replace-ai

    # Get command registry as JSON (for AI)
    bin/list-amos-components --json

=head1 IMPLEMENTATION STATUS

    [NOT IMPLEMENTED YET]

    Planned for next session:
    - Parse inline command metadata from zenka modules
    - Build command registry (command → metadata)
    - Support filtering by tag, zenka, search pattern
    - Output formats: human-readable, JSON, YAML
    - Integration with 'describe' command

=head1 METADATA FORMAT

Commands register themselves via inline metadata blocks:

    ## [:< command-metadata
    #  command  = work.ncode-replace
    #  descr    = Replace text patterns using ncode
    #  usage    = work ncode-replace <target> <search> <replace>
    #  features = auto-confirms, structured output, full backups
    #  tag      = development-tool, code-transformation, ai-friendly
    #  related  = describe, list-amos-components
    ## ]>

=head1 SEE ALSO

    bin/describe - Show full documentation for a command
    bin/ncode - Code transformation and analysis tool
    Configuration: configuration/zenki/work/source/inline-documentation-plan.md

=cut

